{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q250280","formula":"Ca₉Si₆O₁₆(OH)₁₀·6H₂O","hill":"Ca9H22O32Si6","elements":["H","O","Si","Ca"],"composition":{"H":22.0,"O":32.0,"Ca":9.0,"Si":6.0},"names":{"en":"Jennite","uk":"Дженіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Jennite is a calcium silicate hydrate mineral of general chemical formula: Ca9Si6O18(OH)6·8H2O. Jennite occurs as an alteration mineral in metamorphosed limestone and skarn. It typically occurs as vein and open space fillings as a late mineral phase. It also occurs in hydrated cement paste.","uk":"Дженіт — це мінерал гідрату силікату кальцію із загальної хімічною формулою Ca 9 Si 6 O 18 ( OH ) 6 ⋅ 8 H 2 O {\\displaystyle {\\ce {Ca9Si6O18(OH)6*8H2O}}} . Дженіт трапляється як мінерал альтерації в метаморфізованому вапняку та скарні. Зазвичай трапляється у вигляді жилок та заповнень відкритих порожнин як пізня стадія мінералоутворення."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q250280","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jennite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%94%D0%B6%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jennite.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q2518702","formula":"Ca₃[SiO₃(OH)]₂·2H₂O","names":{"en":"Afwillite","ru":"Афвиллит","uk":"Афвіліт"},"elements":["H","O","Si","Ca"],"fame":17,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q13114","formula":"Ca₂[SiO₃(OH)]F·H₂O","names":{"en":"Bultfonteinite","uk":"Бултфонтейніт"},"elements":["H","O","F","Si","Ca"],"fame":12,"kind":null},{"id":"Q3874330